<title>DENMARK: CYCLING-HENN WINS THIRD STAGE OF TOUR OF DENMARK.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-HENN WINS THIRD STAGE OF TOUR OF DENMARK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christian Henn of Germany won the 120-km third stage of the Tour of Denmark cycling race between Nordborg and Haderslev on Friday.</p>
<p>Giovanni Lombardi of Italy, who won Thursday's stage, took over the yellow jersey as overall leader from Australia's Robbie McEwen.</p>
<p>Henn and Lombardi are both with the six-man German Telekom team.</p>
<p>The 859 km race ends in Copenhagen on August 10.</p>
